WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:02.936
- The reason that True the
Vote's research, I think,

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:04.771
is so powerful here is
they set such a high bar,

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.906 align:start size:84% position:16%
10 or more drop
boxes, because, see,

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:09.309
let's say that they had set
a bar of two drop boxes.

00:00:09.309 --> 00:00:10.944 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now, nobody has a
reason to go to two.

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:12.979 align:start size:88% position:13%
Even if you have your
family members' ballots,

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.647
you're gonna go put
'em in one drop box,

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:16.616 align:start size:97% position:3%
but some guy was gonna
come forward and say, well,

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:17.851
you know what?

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:19.085
I put my ballots
in the first box.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:20.887
I had to tie my shoe
at the second box.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.722
So, you're calling me
a mule. I'm not a mule.

00:00:22.722 --> 00:00:24.290
So instead of all this nonsense,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.826
set a bar of 10 or
more drop boxes.

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.995
Let's remember, these aren't,
this isn't the Post Office.

00:00:28.995 --> 00:00:30.897
This isn't where you go
to drop your bills off.

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.399
These are only for ballots.

00:00:32.399 --> 00:00:34.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's no other reason
to go to these drop boxes,

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.702
other than to dump ballots.

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:37.504
And why would you go to
10 or more drop boxes

00:00:37.504 --> 00:00:40.206 align:start size:88% position:13%
unless you were stuffing
them with ballots?

00:00:40.206 --> 00:00:42.675
(funky music)

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.616 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin, and joining
me today is an author,

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:54.487 line:0%
podcast host and creator of
the new film, "2000 Mules,"

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.022
which is out right now.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:58.892 align:start size:97% position:3%
Dinesh D'Souza, welcome
back to "The Rubin Report."

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.427
- Dave, it's a real pleasure.

00:01:00.427 --> 00:01:02.328
Thanks for having me back.
I'm looking forward to it.

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:05.865 align:start size:97% position:3%
- It's been a couple years
since we've chatted on camera,

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:08.401
my friend, but I feel that
we have to give a warning

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:09.936
right up top here.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:12.906
There is a good chance that
my channel will be blown up

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.808
on YouTube because of this.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:17.710
But, I did create Locals.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:19.879
You launched "2000
Mules" on Locals,

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.247
which I obviously
wanna get into.

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.216 align:start size:81% position:19%
And I'm honored
that you did that.

00:01:23.216 --> 00:01:26.152
And anything that we
cannot put on YouTube

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:28.321 align:start size:84% position:16%
for this interview,
we will put up,

00:01:28.321 --> 00:01:29.823
well, I'll just say it,

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:31.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
we'll put it up on both
our channels, fair enough?

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:34.160 line:0%
- I mean, Dave, what a
surreal time we live in.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.763 align:start position:0% line:0%
I don't think you and I
would've predicted a decade ago

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:39.065 line:0%
that we would find that
these basic liberties,

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:41.734 align:start position:0%
which are supposed to be
outside the bounds of politics,

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.536
free speech rights, for example,

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.605 align:start size:84% position:16%
would somehow be
abridged in this way,

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.808 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we'd have to watch
what we say and figure out,

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.310
should I put this up?

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:52.512 align:start size:97% position:3%
I have exactly the same
issue with my daily podcast.

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:54.848
And with this movie, you know,

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.716 align:start size:84% position:16%
I couldn't put the
trailer up on YouTube.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.318
I couldn't buy ads on Facebook.

00:01:58.318 --> 00:02:01.254 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, had to develop an entirely
different business plan

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:02.622
for releasing this movie

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.824
as compared to any
of my earlier ones.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:07.594 align:start position:0%
- So, let's get into that
business plan in just a moment.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:10.029
But first, let's focus
on the movie itself.

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:12.198
I was at the,

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.634
I suppose it was the pre
premiere of the movie,

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:18.071
which was at Mar-a-Lago, and
it was sort of a who's who

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:20.340 line:0%
of let's say right wing media,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.710 line:0%
or whatever you wanna call
all of us at this point.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:24.811
And I got to see the movie.

00:02:24.811 --> 00:02:26.045
I thought it was excellent.

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.914
Many people on my book tour,

00:02:27.914 --> 00:02:29.949
one of the questions that I
got more than anything else

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.151
over the last couple weeks was,

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:32.519
what did you think of the movie?

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.454 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I recommended
that everyone see it,

00:02:34.454 --> 00:02:36.456 align:start size:84% position:16%
make some judgements
for themselves.

00:02:36.456 --> 00:02:40.593 align:start size:97% position:3%
What was the initial
starting point of when you,

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you wanna immediately
ask questions,

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.930
like the night of the election?

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.498
Or was it a couple weeks later?

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:48.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
What was sort of the
genesis of the whole idea?

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:49.235
- Well, like a lot of people,

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:52.605
I noticed the anomalies of 2020,

00:02:52.605 --> 00:02:56.309
and they struck me as really
strange, but once the curtain,

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:59.179 align:start position:0%
well, once Biden was
inaugurated and then, of course,

00:02:59.179 --> 00:03:02.248 align:start position:0%
a curtain of censorship descends
on this topic, I thought,

00:03:02.248 --> 00:03:04.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
man, you know, we probably
will never find out

00:03:04.751 --> 00:03:06.753
what really happened
in the 2020 election.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:10.423
With each passing day, the
event becomes more remote,

00:03:10.423 --> 00:03:13.426
and I was dissatisfied with
the rhetoric a little bit

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:14.594
on both sides.

00:03:14.594 --> 00:03:15.895 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now, you know,
start with the left,

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.131 align:start size:84% position:16%
the most secure
election in history.

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:19.566
And I thought to myself,

00:03:19.566 --> 00:03:21.868 align:start size:97% position:3%
even before I started anything
with "2000 Mules," well,

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.503 align:start size:84% position:16%
how could you
possibly know that?

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:24.437 align:start size:84% position:16%
And they'd be
like, well, Dinesh,

00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:25.805
where's your proof of fraud?

00:03:25.805 --> 00:03:27.307
And I'm like, well,
let's say I had none.

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:28.775
I have no proof.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.643 align:start size:97% position:3%
Does it make it the most
secure election of all time?

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:31.844
I mean -

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:32.612 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right, these are
still separate things.

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.347
- Yeah.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:35.815
You haven't done an
actual comparison of
the amount of fraud

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.550 align:start size:88% position:13%
in the last seven
elections, for example,

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:40.119 align:start size:84% position:16%
to show me that it
was the least in 2020,

00:03:40.119 --> 00:03:41.988
and yet, that became the mantra.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.456
Now, on the conservative side,

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:48.261
as you know, a lot of flying
theories going about anomalies,

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.729
episodic fraud, I mean,

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.331
look at this dead guy
who voted over here,

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:53.499 align:start size:97% position:3%
look at that guy was
stuffing ballots over there.

00:03:53.499 --> 00:03:56.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
But of course, the courts
in these situations

00:03:56.469 --> 00:04:00.273
use the principle that can be
called the but for principle,

00:04:00.273 --> 00:04:01.874
but for the fraud,

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.509
would the election have
come out differently?

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.978
And that's a pretty high bar.

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:07.680 align:start size:97% position:3%
You have to show a magnitude
of fraud, and that was,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.883 align:start position:0%
I had never felt was really
done, never shown, never proven.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.319 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so, again, I
thought, let's move on.

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.355
This is something that
we might never know.

00:04:15.355 --> 00:04:17.056 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, it wasn't until
I sat down with

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:20.326
the two principles
of the organization
called True the Vote

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:22.228
that I realized that they
had sort of approached

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:24.864
the election like a cold
case, like cold case files.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.099
And they figured out, you know,

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.967
there actually is
a way to go back

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:31.971
and track the movements
of these so-called mules.

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:35.241 align:start position:0%
And there is a way also to look,
through surveillance video,

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:38.478
and in a sense, take us
back to the days before

00:04:38.478 --> 00:04:40.280
and during the 2020 election

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:43.516 align:start size:97% position:3%
to actually see what happened
with your own two eyes.

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:46.185
- Okay, so, before we get
into some of the specifics

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:47.820
of how they used geo tagging

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:49.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
and how they were actually
tracking these mules,

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:51.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I want you to actually
define what a mule is,

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:53.159
which you do in the
movie, obviously,

00:04:53.159 --> 00:04:55.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
how do you as a filmmaker,
'cause you've obviously

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.796 align:start size:84% position:16%
made a bunch of
documentaries before,

00:04:56.796 --> 00:05:00.833
how do you make sure that
your own personal opinions

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:03.169 line:0%
don't override the truth?

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:05.471 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
Because, to me, that's
gotta be the hardest part.

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:07.073 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
I think there are
moments in the movie

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:08.875 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
where you sort of address
that a little bit,

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:11.944 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
but to remove all of
your bias, for all of us,

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.480
is almost completely impossible.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:15.748
- It is impossible.

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:17.884
And I would argue that
in terms of attaining

00:05:17.884 --> 00:05:20.486 align:start size:97% position:3%
that kind of pure objectivity,
that's never gonna happen.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:22.955 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, that doesn't
occur at all,

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:25.391
but what you can
do is try to have

00:05:25.391 --> 00:05:27.994
that sort of empathetic ability,

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.996
and it's a debating
ability, by the way,

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:32.632
to always see the strength
of the counter argument,

00:05:32.632 --> 00:05:34.167
of the other guy's point of view

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:36.336
and import that into the film.

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:38.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
Also, one of my
techniques here was,

00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:41.574
I recognize that among the
kind of Salem podcast hosts,

00:05:41.574 --> 00:05:44.844
I'm thinking of people like
Eric Metaxas and Larry Elder,

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
there were a mix of
views about the election.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:48.848 align:start size:84% position:16%
Some of them, it
was stolen for sure.

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:51.417 align:start size:97% position:3%
Some of them, nah, I haven't
seen any proof of it.

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:54.954 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I had the idea of
importing them into the movie,

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.656
having their initial thoughts,

00:05:56.656 --> 00:05:58.091
then showing them the evidence

00:05:58.091 --> 00:06:00.426 align:start size:97% position:3%
and literally spontaneously
filming their reaction

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:02.228
and then asking them
for their assessments.

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.429
I thought, in this way,

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.098
it goes beyond just
sort of Dinesh's

00:06:05.098 --> 00:06:06.899
singular interpretation.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:09.302 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it becomes a
conversation about the issue

00:06:09.302 --> 00:06:10.636 align:start size:84% position:16%
in which it's
possible that somebody

00:06:10.636 --> 00:06:12.138
watching the movie
would go, you know,

00:06:12.138 --> 00:06:15.141
I see stronger ground in
what Larry Elder is saying

00:06:15.141 --> 00:06:16.676 align:start size:84% position:16%
than anything Dinesh
might have said.

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:20.179
So, by doing it that way, it
does what a good movie does,

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:23.449 align:start size:84% position:16%
which is, it lays
out a narrative with
a range of positions

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:26.285 align:start size:97% position:3%
and a range of potential,
of possible interpretations.

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:27.320
- It was interesting.

00:06:28.721 --> 00:06:30.223 align:start size:97% position:3%
So, you use this round table
of the Salem hosts, so,

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:34.260
it's you and Dennis Prager and
Larry Elder and Eric Metaxas

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:35.795
and Charlie Kirk.

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:37.230
Am I forgetting anyone?

00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:38.464
Oh, and Seb Gorka.

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:39.699
- And Gorka, yeah.

00:06:39.699 --> 00:06:41.701 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Again, and you guys
sort of spurt, you know,

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:43.736
you guys come and go
throughout the movie,

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.338
discussing what's going on.

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:46.873 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it's interesting
because Dennis,

00:06:46.873 --> 00:06:49.509 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think, comes off as the most
skeptical at the beginning.

00:06:49.509 --> 00:06:51.177 align:start size:88% position:13%
He kind of comes around
a little bit more,

00:06:51.177 --> 00:06:53.513
but everyone's asking
questions throughout

00:06:53.513 --> 00:06:55.648 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, obviously, you
didn't cut the questions.

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:58.151
So, there's some credit there.

00:06:58.151 --> 00:06:59.786
- I mean, in some ways
that's the best part,

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:01.187
where Dennis will
say, for example,

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:02.655 align:start size:84% position:16%
hey, listen, you
know, you have a mule,

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:04.157
you're showing this
guy stuffing ballots.

00:07:04.157 --> 00:07:06.759 align:start size:97% position:3%
What if you run up to him
right now and grab his ballots

00:07:06.759 --> 00:07:08.895 align:start size:97% position:3%
and look at them, what
would you see on the ballot?

00:07:08.895 --> 00:07:11.631
I mean, what's cool about it
to me is, I thought to myself,

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.166
those are the kinds of
questions that people

00:07:13.166 --> 00:07:14.500
in the audience are
gonna be asking.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.836
So, by putting them
right in the movie,

00:07:16.836 --> 00:07:18.571
the movie doesn't
have to come back

00:07:18.571 --> 00:07:21.107
and answer those questions
because they are anticipated

00:07:21.107 --> 00:07:24.644
and addressed and at least
discussed in the film itself.

00:07:24.644 --> 00:07:26.879
- Okay, so, for the people
that have not seen it yet,

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:29.715
without blowing anything
major, can you at least,

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:33.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
can you give the kind
of elevator pitch
on the methodology

00:07:33.352 --> 00:07:35.254
that you guys were looking at

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:38.291 align:start position:0%
related to people's smartphones
and where they were going

00:07:38.291 --> 00:07:42.695 align:start size:97% position:3%
and just the, the basic idea
of what "2000 Mules" is?

00:07:42.695 --> 00:07:45.898
- Sure, the film, drawing
on the work of this group

00:07:45.898 --> 00:07:48.401
called True the Vote, a kind
of election intelligence group,

00:07:48.401 --> 00:07:52.972 align:start size:84% position:16%
if you will, uses
two independent modes
of investigation

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:54.407
or two modes of argument.

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:56.742
The first one is cell
phone geo tracking,

00:07:56.742 --> 00:07:59.145
and that arises out
at the simple point

00:07:59.145 --> 00:08:01.347
that we're at a stage
of technology now,

00:08:01.347 --> 00:08:03.483
and perhaps also a stage
where we have relinquished

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:05.518
our privacy to a point now

00:08:05.518 --> 00:08:08.688 align:start size:84% position:16%
where our movements
can be tracked.

00:08:08.688 --> 00:08:11.457
They're tracked because of, not
because of cell phone towers

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:14.627 align:start size:97% position:3%
that are pinging, it's because
of apps inside our phone

00:08:14.627 --> 00:08:17.697 align:start position:0%
that allow so-called aggregators
to collect this data.

00:08:17.697 --> 00:08:19.532 align:start size:88% position:13%
And, by the way, it's
sold on the open market.

00:08:19.532 --> 00:08:21.200
Commercial companies can buy it.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:22.435
It's also very valuable

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:24.237 align:start size:84% position:16%
to law enforcement,
intelligence agencies,

00:08:24.237 --> 00:08:27.206
but, essentially, if I was
being geo tracked right now,

00:08:27.206 --> 00:08:28.875
you could tell for sure,

00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:31.577 align:start size:84% position:16%
I woke up in my
bedroom in my house.

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:33.045
I then went to a coffee shop.

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:34.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then, I went to the studio
to record my podcast,

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I had lunch with a
friend at this restaurant.

00:08:36.549 --> 00:08:39.118
Then, I came home, and
all of that is shown,

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:41.053 align:start size:84% position:16%
not by a single
snapshot of my phone,

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:42.622
but by what's called
a pattern of life.

00:08:42.622 --> 00:08:44.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're showing the
movement of my cell phone.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:47.426
Now, obviously, if I gave my
cell phone to my wife, Debbie,

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:48.928
it would show her movements,

00:08:48.928 --> 00:08:51.030
but that the cell phone
is making these movements

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.966
and going to these locations
is really not open to doubt.

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:56.269
And so, what True the
Vote did is they used

00:08:56.269 --> 00:08:59.305
the cell phone geo tracking
used in many other areas.

00:08:59.305 --> 00:09:00.940
Their kind of genius idea was,

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.543
let's apply that to
ballot trafficking.

00:09:03.543 --> 00:09:05.545
And what we're looking
for are these mules.

00:09:05.545 --> 00:09:06.979
Now, what's a mule?

00:09:06.979 --> 00:09:10.449 align:start size:97% position:3%
Basically, a paid operative
who is handed ballots

00:09:10.449 --> 00:09:13.252
and asked to drop them
off, to deliver them

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:15.655
to mail in drop boxes.

00:09:15.655 --> 00:09:19.792 align:start position:0%
And we've been able to
identify, based on a criterion,

00:09:19.792 --> 00:09:21.360
actually, a very high criterion,

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:24.764
mules going to 10
or more drop boxes,

00:09:24.764 --> 00:09:26.432
some 2000 mules,

00:09:26.432 --> 00:09:28.935
and that's where the title
of the movie comes from.

00:09:28.935 --> 00:09:31.170
- Right, so, you believe
that there are way more

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.371
than 2000 mules,

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:34.106 align:start size:84% position:16%
but you were just
focusing on this group

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:36.676 align:start size:88% position:13%
that had this very
sort of high threshold.

00:09:36.676 --> 00:09:38.110
And as you show in the movie,

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.879 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, a lot of these
people that were repeatedly

00:09:39.879 --> 00:09:42.915
going to these drop
boxes, they, I mean,

00:09:42.915 --> 00:09:45.918
they look like transients
or almost homeless people.

00:09:45.918 --> 00:09:49.822 align:start size:97% position:3%
A lot of them, they're showing
up at 4:00 AM and 7:00 AM.

00:09:49.822 --> 00:09:51.691
They kind of look disheveled.

00:09:51.691 --> 00:09:53.392
They, in other words,

00:09:53.392 --> 00:09:56.395
they don't look like sort
of the upstanding citizen

00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:59.398
that's doing their due
service for the country

00:09:59.398 --> 00:10:01.901
because they've collected
some ballots for, you know,

00:10:01.901 --> 00:10:03.202
some people that
can't, you know,

00:10:03.202 --> 00:10:04.604
drop the ballots off themselves.

00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:07.306
It doesn't come off
exactly like that.

00:10:07.306 --> 00:10:08.441
- Exactly.

00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:09.909 align:start size:88% position:13%
Now, in the five
states that we look at,

00:10:09.909 --> 00:10:13.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is Georgia, Arizona,
Wisconsin, Michigan,

00:10:13.646 --> 00:10:16.248
and Pennsylvania, you
don't have the kind of

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:18.718 align:start size:97% position:3%
liberal vote harvesting where
you can give your ballot

00:10:18.718 --> 00:10:20.586
to anyone and have
them drop it off.

00:10:20.586 --> 00:10:22.722
That is the case, by
the way, in California.

00:10:22.722 --> 00:10:23.990
But even in California,

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:25.825
you can't pay people
to deliver ballots.

00:10:25.825 --> 00:10:27.760 align:start size:97% position:3%
I can't say to my neighbor,
go drop off my ballot,

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.396
and here's 50 bucks, because
the moment money comes in,

00:10:30.396 --> 00:10:31.564
there's bribery.

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:33.032 align:start size:84% position:16%
Essentially, the
vote is contaminated,

00:10:33.032 --> 00:10:35.267 align:start size:84% position:16%
and even a legal
vote becomes illegal

00:10:35.267 --> 00:10:36.936
when money changes hands.

00:10:36.936 --> 00:10:38.871
Now, in places like
Georgia and Arizona,

00:10:38.871 --> 00:10:42.241
you can only give your ballot
to an immediate family member,

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:44.510 align:start size:88% position:13%
or if you are confined,
to a caregiver.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:46.012
That's it.

00:10:46.012 --> 00:10:47.647
And I think you can see, this
is the power of the video.

00:10:47.647 --> 00:10:50.616
The second line of evidence in
the movie is you begin to see

00:10:50.616 --> 00:10:51.951
not just cell phone devices

00:10:51.951 --> 00:10:53.386 align:start size:84% position:16%
moving from one
drop box to another,

00:10:53.386 --> 00:10:55.121 align:start size:84% position:16%
but you actually get
to see the mules.

00:10:55.121 --> 00:10:56.489
And I think it's very telling,

00:10:56.489 --> 00:10:58.891
because when you see a
guy jump out of a car

00:10:58.891 --> 00:11:00.826
at three in the morning,
he looks left and right,

00:11:00.826 --> 00:11:02.294 align:start size:84% position:16%
makes sure no one's
looking at him.

00:11:02.294 --> 00:11:04.830 align:start size:88% position:13%
It has all the hallmarks
to any observer

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:07.767
that this is an illicit
and nefarious operation

00:11:07.767 --> 00:11:10.102 align:start size:84% position:16%
being conducted
under cover of night.

00:11:10.102 --> 00:11:12.905
- Okay, so, even for someone
that hasn't seen the movie yet,

00:11:12.905 --> 00:11:14.173
they're hearing you.

00:11:14.173 --> 00:11:15.408
They're going, okay, so,
let's get this straight.

00:11:15.408 --> 00:11:16.909
These guys have the phones.

00:11:16.909 --> 00:11:19.545
We're tracking these people.
They're showing up repeatedly.

00:11:19.545 --> 00:11:21.681 align:start size:88% position:13%
They look kind of
shady. You've got video.

00:11:21.681 --> 00:11:23.282
Now some of them
are wearing masks

00:11:23.282 --> 00:11:24.884
'cause it was also during COVID

00:11:24.884 --> 00:11:26.519 align:start size:84% position:16%
or they were
disguising themselves.

00:11:26.519 --> 00:11:29.021 align:start size:88% position:13%
But, a bunch of them,
you can see their faces.

00:11:29.021 --> 00:11:32.391
So, clearly we can figure
out who these people are.

00:11:32.391 --> 00:11:34.226
So, what kind of
work have you done,

00:11:34.226 --> 00:11:37.930 align:start size:88% position:13%
or is ongoing to figure
out who they are.

00:11:37.930 --> 00:11:40.533 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I guess the real
question is, who paid them?

00:11:40.533 --> 00:11:45.004
- Right, so they, when you
see these mules operating,

00:11:45.004 --> 00:11:47.473 align:start size:84% position:16%
you see that they
stop at organizations,

00:11:47.473 --> 00:11:49.041 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
and that's where
they get the ballots.

00:11:49.041 --> 00:11:50.843 line:0%
So, the mules don't come
up with their own ballots.

00:11:50.843 --> 00:11:53.446 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
They go to what we
call vote stash houses.

00:11:53.446 --> 00:11:54.947 line:0%
And what are they?

00:11:54.947 --> 00:11:57.583 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, they turn out to be kind
of far left organizations,

00:11:57.583 --> 00:11:59.285 align:start size:81% position:19%
deeply embedded
in the inner city,

00:11:59.285 --> 00:12:02.688 align:start size:84% position:16%
places like Atlanta,
Philadelphia,
Detroit, and so on.

00:12:02.688 --> 00:12:03.889
So, they go to these places.

00:12:03.889 --> 00:12:04.824 align:start size:84% position:16%
They get the ballots,
and then they -

00:12:04.824 --> 00:12:06.125
- Wait, to be clear though,

00:12:06.125 --> 00:12:07.793 align:start size:88% position:13%
'cause you actually show
the map in the movie,

00:12:07.793 --> 00:12:10.996
you show them actually
going to these places

00:12:10.996 --> 00:12:14.400
before they're doing
the drop off, actually.

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:15.835
- Yeah, not only that,

00:12:15.835 --> 00:12:17.703 align:start size:94% position:6%
but once they go to
three or four drop boxes,

00:12:17.703 --> 00:12:18.938
they need to get more ballots,

00:12:18.938 --> 00:12:20.606
so they go right back
to the organization,

00:12:20.606 --> 00:12:22.341 align:start size:84% position:16%
sort of replenish, and
then they continue.

00:12:22.341 --> 00:12:24.243
Now, it's important to
say why they do this,

00:12:24.243 --> 00:12:25.377 align:start size:84% position:16%
because you'd think,
wait a minute,

00:12:25.377 --> 00:12:27.113 align:start size:84% position:16%
if a mule is
dumping 300 ballots,

00:12:27.113 --> 00:12:29.281 align:start size:97% position:3%
why don't you go to one drop
box and just unload them,

00:12:29.281 --> 00:12:31.317 align:start size:84% position:16%
save yourself a whole
bunch of trouble.

00:12:31.317 --> 00:12:33.018 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, the reason is
that the next morning,

00:12:33.018 --> 00:12:35.421
the election officials
open these drop boxes.

00:12:35.421 --> 00:12:38.190 align:start size:97% position:3%
And let's say the typical
drop box has like 80 ballots,

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.793
and then this one drop
box has like 700 ballots.

00:12:40.793 --> 00:12:42.495 align:start size:84% position:16%
You'd know right
away something is up.

00:12:42.495 --> 00:12:44.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, the mules are
instructed not to do that.

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:46.632 align:start size:97% position:3%
They drop five ballots here
or eight ballots there.

00:12:46.632 --> 00:12:48.200
That's why they go
on these routes,

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:50.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that, of course, makes
them easier to track.

00:12:50.369 --> 00:12:53.105
The reason that True the
Vote's research, I think,

00:12:53.105 --> 00:12:55.007
is so powerful here is
they set such a high bar,

00:12:55.007 --> 00:12:57.143 align:start size:84% position:16%
10 or more drop
boxes, because, see,

00:12:57.143 --> 00:12:59.578
let's say that they had set
a bar of two drop boxes.

00:12:59.578 --> 00:13:01.080 align:start size:84% position:16%
Now, nobody has a
reason to go to two.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.082 align:start size:88% position:13%
Even if you have your
family members' ballots,

00:13:03.082 --> 00:13:04.784
you're gonna go put
'em in one drop box.

00:13:04.784 --> 00:13:06.752 align:start size:97% position:3%
But some guy was gonna
come forward and say, well,

00:13:06.752 --> 00:13:09.221
you know what, I put my
ballots in the first box.

00:13:09.221 --> 00:13:10.990
I had to tie my shoe
at the second box.

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:12.892
So, you're calling me
a mule. I'm not a mule.

00:13:12.892 --> 00:13:14.126 align:start size:81% position:19%
So, instead of
all this nonsense,

00:13:14.126 --> 00:13:16.962
set a bar of 10 or
more drop boxes.

00:13:16.962 --> 00:13:19.131
Let's remember these aren't,
this isn't the Post Office.

00:13:19.131 --> 00:13:21.033
This isn't where you go
to drop your bills off.

00:13:21.033 --> 00:13:22.568
These are only for ballots.

00:13:22.568 --> 00:13:24.303
There's no other reason
to go to these drop boxes

00:13:24.303 --> 00:13:25.805
other than to dump ballots.

00:13:25.805 --> 00:13:28.040
And why would you go to
10 or more drop boxes

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.742 align:start size:88% position:13%
unless you were stuffing
them with ballots?

00:13:29.742 --> 00:13:32.711
So, that's the sort of
technological reasoning

00:13:32.711 --> 00:13:34.914
behind the power of the
geo tracking evidence.

00:13:34.914 --> 00:13:37.650 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now, I wish we had more video,
but True the Vote does have

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:38.984
4 million minutes of video.

00:13:38.984 --> 00:13:40.519
So they have a lot,

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:43.756
but unfortunately, a lot of
drop boxes don't have video.

00:13:43.756 --> 00:13:46.225 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Right, so, are they going
through more video now?

00:13:46.225 --> 00:13:48.327 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because there is,
you have some people,

00:13:48.327 --> 00:13:49.795
you have their faces, I mean,

00:13:49.795 --> 00:13:52.231
have they been doing any
work to track these people?

00:13:52.231 --> 00:13:54.366
Do you know where any
of these people are?

00:13:54.366 --> 00:13:57.169
I mean, again, a lot of them
sort of seem like transients

00:13:57.169 --> 00:14:00.806 align:start position:0%
or just probably unidentifiable
for one reason or another,

00:14:00.806 --> 00:14:03.709
but there's gotta be some way
to get some of them, right?

00:14:03.709 --> 00:14:04.810
- Well, here's the key point.

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:05.778
I mean, obviously you're right.

00:14:05.778 --> 00:14:07.246
Some of these mules are visible.

00:14:07.246 --> 00:14:09.615 align:start position:0%
You can see their face, and
they can be recognized that way.

00:14:09.615 --> 00:14:11.550 align:start size:97% position:3%
But the more important thing
is that True the Vote has

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:16.121
the cell phone IDs of all the
mules, all the 2000 mules.

00:14:16.121 --> 00:14:17.656
So, when you track a cell phone,

00:14:17.656 --> 00:14:20.159
each cell phone has a unique
kind of digital fingerprint,

00:14:20.159 --> 00:14:21.293
the cell phone ID.

00:14:21.293 --> 00:14:22.995
Each cell phone has only one ID.

00:14:22.995 --> 00:14:25.397 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it's about as good,
technologically, as having,

00:14:25.397 --> 00:14:29.001 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, a finger, human
fingerprint or even human DNA.

00:14:29.001 --> 00:14:31.203 align:start size:84% position:16%
It has the same
degree of reliability.

00:14:31.203 --> 00:14:34.139 align:start size:88% position:13%
Now, interestingly, True
the Vote doesn't have

00:14:34.139 --> 00:14:35.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
the names of these mules,
but law enforcement,

00:14:35.908 --> 00:14:39.078
they unmask these cell
phones all the time.

00:14:39.078 --> 00:14:41.480
So, unmasking simply means you
go to a judge, you say, hey,

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.916
listen, I've got these guys
at 10 or more drop boxes,

00:14:43.916 --> 00:14:45.384
so I have probable cause.

00:14:45.384 --> 00:14:46.819
The judge goes,
here's a warrant.

00:14:46.819 --> 00:14:48.254 align:start size:81% position:19%
You go to the cell
phone provider.

00:14:48.254 --> 00:14:49.655 align:start size:88% position:13%
They give you the
names of all the mules,

00:14:49.655 --> 00:14:50.856
and then you go interview them.

00:14:50.856 --> 00:14:51.790
You know, who paid you,

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.192
who put you up to it and so on.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:56.428
- So where are you
at in that process?

00:14:56.428 --> 00:14:58.030
- So, where we are
is that True the Vote

00:14:58.030 --> 00:14:59.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
has been working hard
with the state of Georgia,

00:14:59.932 --> 00:15:03.168
but there's a very subtle
and complex investigation,

00:15:03.168 --> 00:15:05.204
and it's not clear that
the secretary of state,

00:15:05.204 --> 00:15:07.773 align:start size:97% position:3%
Raffensperger, who's
leading this investigation,

00:15:07.773 --> 00:15:09.942 align:start size:88% position:13%
is trying to push it
forward or hold it back.

00:15:09.942 --> 00:15:13.178 align:start position:0%
He's involved in a very complex
politics inside of Georgia.

00:15:13.178 --> 00:15:16.181
Now, in Yuma County, Arizona,
the sheriff just announced,

00:15:16.181 --> 00:15:18.817 align:start size:97% position:3%
unknown to us, that
there's a new investigation

00:15:18.817 --> 00:15:21.287
into criminal ballot
trafficking in Yuma.

00:15:21.287 --> 00:15:23.522 align:start position:0%
And this is, of course,
important because, in the movie,

00:15:23.522 --> 00:15:24.857
we interview a mule.

00:15:24.857 --> 00:15:25.791
Where is she from?

00:15:25.791 --> 00:15:28.027
San Luis, inside of Yuma County.

00:15:28.027 --> 00:15:30.262
True the Vote has done
work in Yuma for months.

00:15:30.262 --> 00:15:31.597
So while the sheriff goes,

00:15:31.597 --> 00:15:33.732
I'm not doing it because
of a movie, and frankly,

00:15:33.732 --> 00:15:35.634
we wouldn't want him
to say any differently,

00:15:35.634 --> 00:15:37.736
here is a guy who has
been checking into this

00:15:37.736 --> 00:15:39.004
and, in a sense,

00:15:39.004 --> 00:15:40.706
it provides a certain
independent validation

00:15:40.706 --> 00:15:42.274
that this is a legitimate issue.

00:15:42.274 --> 00:15:44.310 align:start size:88% position:13%
This kind of ballot
trafficking does go on,

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.711
and it is a crime.

00:15:45.711 --> 00:15:48.447
- What has been sort
of what you would say

00:15:48.447 --> 00:15:52.284 align:start size:97% position:3%
is the most legit criticism
of the movie that you've seen?

00:15:52.284 --> 00:15:53.919 align:start size:88% position:13%
You know, I've seen a
lot of just sort of, oh,

00:15:53.919 --> 00:15:55.921 align:start size:84% position:16%
here's Dinesh
peddling the big lie.

00:15:55.921 --> 00:15:58.257 align:start size:97% position:3%
Actually, like a minute
before we connected on Skype,

00:15:58.257 --> 00:16:01.694
I saw that you tweeted out,
it was a criticism from,

00:16:01.694 --> 00:16:03.996
I think it was like
a former FBI guy,

00:16:03.996 --> 00:16:06.865 align:start size:97% position:3%
who basically just said,
oh, Dinesh's big lie movie's

00:16:06.865 --> 00:16:07.967
going to the theaters,

00:16:07.967 --> 00:16:09.335 align:start size:88% position:13%
but there's no
criticism of the movie.

00:16:09.335 --> 00:16:11.570 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's just sort of this
blanket criticism,

00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:12.838
but I'm sure you've
heard some things

00:16:12.838 --> 00:16:14.506
that have brought up issues,

00:16:14.506 --> 00:16:17.443 align:start size:97% position:3%
or maybe things that you wish
you addressed, et cetera.

00:16:17.443 --> 00:16:20.612 align:start size:97% position:3%
- There are two very plausible
and legitimate criticisms,

00:16:20.612 --> 00:16:21.880
and I've tried to address both.

00:16:21.880 --> 00:16:23.182 align:start size:81% position:19%
One was brought
up by Megyn Kelly,

00:16:23.182 --> 00:16:26.385
and it was basically this.

00:16:26.385 --> 00:16:28.687
Where do the ballots come from?

00:16:28.687 --> 00:16:29.922
So, in other words,

00:16:29.922 --> 00:16:31.123
we know that they come
from the nonprofits,

00:16:31.123 --> 00:16:32.358
but where do the
nonprofits get 'em?

00:16:32.358 --> 00:16:33.625
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:16:33.625 --> 00:16:35.961
- Are these legal votes
that are being delivered

00:16:35.961 --> 00:16:39.131
in an illegal way, or
are these fraudulent

00:16:39.131 --> 00:16:40.766
and illegal votes
in the first place

00:16:40.766 --> 00:16:43.302 align:start size:97% position:3%
that are also being delivered
in a fraudulent way?

00:16:43.302 --> 00:16:44.937 align:start size:97% position:3%
- And Dennis sort of brings
that up in the movie,

00:16:44.937 --> 00:16:46.171
doesn't he, as well?

00:16:46.171 --> 00:16:48.240
- Yeah, we address this
directly in the movie.

00:16:48.240 --> 00:16:51.210 align:start position:0%
And what we say is, in a
sense, we cannot know for sure,

00:16:51.210 --> 00:16:55.314 align:start size:97% position:3%
because we're tracking the
ballot from the drop box back,

00:16:55.314 --> 00:16:57.883 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we know the origination
point is the nonprofit.

00:16:57.883 --> 00:17:00.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, we know the nonprofits
are paying the mules.

00:17:00.285 --> 00:17:02.254 align:start size:97% position:3%
Now, where do the
nonprofits get the ballots?

00:17:02.254 --> 00:17:03.789
Now, the problem here is this.

00:17:03.789 --> 00:17:06.425 align:start position:0%
I cannot think, if you were
talking about a hundred ballots,

00:17:06.425 --> 00:17:07.860 align:start size:81% position:19%
I could say, well,
you know what,

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
some nonprofit went
through a housing complex,

00:17:09.461 --> 00:17:10.896 align:start size:84% position:16%
they collected
everybody's ballot,

00:17:10.896 --> 00:17:13.065 align:start position:0%
but we're talking about
hundreds of thousands of ballots

00:17:13.065 --> 00:17:15.167
being collected in
five separate states.

00:17:15.167 --> 00:17:16.635
So, I say to myself,

00:17:16.635 --> 00:17:19.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
what is the plausible
scenario of a legal voter,

00:17:19.805 --> 00:17:22.007
say Dave Rubin or Dinesh
saying, you know what?

00:17:22.007 --> 00:17:23.475
I'm feeling a little lazy today.

00:17:23.475 --> 00:17:25.244
I don't want to go down
the mail in drop box,

00:17:25.244 --> 00:17:27.746
I'm gonna go to a left wing
nonprofit in the inner city,

00:17:27.746 --> 00:17:30.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
give them my lawful ballot
so they can hire a mule

00:17:30.682 --> 00:17:32.117 align:start size:84% position:16%
to go in the middle
of the night,

00:17:32.117 --> 00:17:35.054 align:start size:97% position:3%
wearing gloves and take photos
of the ballots going in.

00:17:35.054 --> 00:17:36.488
It makes no sense.

00:17:36.488 --> 00:17:38.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
So there's, I cannot
think of any plausible way

00:17:38.357 --> 00:17:40.192 align:start size:81% position:19%
for these to be
all legal ballots.

00:17:40.192 --> 00:17:43.362
So, my guess is it's a mixture
of legal and illegal ballots,

00:17:43.362 --> 00:17:45.831
but all these ballots
are rendered fraudulent

00:17:45.831 --> 00:17:48.300
by the simple fact that
the mules are being paid,

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:51.537
and that paid ballot
trafficking is illegal

00:17:51.537 --> 00:17:52.871
in all 50 states.

00:17:52.871 --> 00:17:54.807
- So, you mentioned the
take a picture thing.

00:17:54.807 --> 00:17:56.475 align:start size:84% position:16%
So, that is one of
the interesting things

00:17:56.475 --> 00:17:58.811
that many times,
almost every time,

00:17:58.811 --> 00:18:00.879
the way they get paid is
they have to take a picture

00:18:00.879 --> 00:18:02.648 align:start size:81% position:19%
as they're putting
the ballots in.

00:18:02.648 --> 00:18:04.516
Otherwise, obviously,
for all they know,

00:18:04.516 --> 00:18:05.984
the nonprofit thinks

00:18:05.984 --> 00:18:07.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they're just dumping
the ballot somewhere.

00:18:07.486 --> 00:18:10.889
Would there be any other
reason to take a picture?

00:18:10.889 --> 00:18:14.460
I mean, is there any reason
someone might take, I mean,

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:17.463
other than for Instagram
purposes or something?

00:18:17.463 --> 00:18:18.697
- Well, this is the key point.

00:18:18.697 --> 00:18:20.632 align:start size:84% position:16%
So Washington Post,
Philip Bump and others

00:18:20.632 --> 00:18:21.900
have basically said,

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:24.002
it's not uncommon for
people to take selfies

00:18:24.002 --> 00:18:25.504
to show that they voted.

00:18:25.504 --> 00:18:27.139
They're really proud
of their citizenship.

00:18:27.139 --> 00:18:29.408
They wanna show that
they've participated,

00:18:29.408 --> 00:18:31.810 align:start size:97% position:3%
but see, that involves
taking a picture of yourself.

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:33.312
- Right, 'cause, right.

00:18:33.312 --> 00:18:36.515 align:start position:0%
- In the movie, you see the
mule standing behind the camera,

00:18:36.515 --> 00:18:38.750 align:start size:84% position:16%
taking a photo of
the ballot going in.

00:18:38.750 --> 00:18:41.186 align:start position:0%
So, again, you have to, and
the same thing with the gloves.

00:18:41.186 --> 00:18:43.922
If there were gloves from
early voting, October 1,

00:18:43.922 --> 00:18:46.725 align:start size:97% position:3%
all the way through the
Georgia runoffs, January 5th,

00:18:46.725 --> 00:18:48.393 align:start size:84% position:16%
then you'd go, well,
maybe it's COVID.

00:18:48.393 --> 00:18:50.095
But when you see that
there are no gloves

00:18:50.095 --> 00:18:52.464 align:start size:97% position:3%
all the way in early
voting and on election day,

00:18:52.464 --> 00:18:55.000
and the gloves only show
up in the Georgia runoffs

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.836 align:start size:88% position:13%
immediately following
an indictment in Arizona

00:18:57.836 --> 00:19:00.806 align:start size:97% position:3%
where the FBI busts a criminal
ring of ballot traffickers

00:19:00.806 --> 00:19:03.742 align:start size:97% position:3%
by finding their fingerprints
on multiple ballots.

00:19:03.742 --> 00:19:07.312 align:start size:97% position:3%
Well, which theory is a better
explanation of those facts?

00:19:07.312 --> 00:19:09.882 align:start size:97% position:3%
The COVID theory or the
theory that the word went out

00:19:09.882 --> 00:19:11.150
among the mules,

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.985
guys, you better start
wearing latex gloves?

00:19:12.985 --> 00:19:15.521
- What should we know
about these nonprofits

00:19:15.521 --> 00:19:18.557 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sort of where they're
getting their funding

00:19:18.557 --> 00:19:21.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
and are they coordinating
it with each other?

00:19:21.126 --> 00:19:22.761
I mean, are they, is
this just, you know,

00:19:22.761 --> 00:19:24.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
these happen to be a
bunch of left wing things

00:19:24.796 --> 00:19:27.065
that are all kind of
doing the same thing?

00:19:27.065 --> 00:19:29.668 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, do we know how
connected they are?

00:19:29.668 --> 00:19:31.403
- Well, what's really
interesting, Dave,

00:19:31.403 --> 00:19:34.139 align:start size:97% position:3%
and we have Scott Walter
from Capital Research Center,

00:19:34.139 --> 00:19:35.641
in the movie, talks about this.

00:19:35.641 --> 00:19:38.710
A big river of cash goes to
these left wing nonprofits

00:19:38.710 --> 00:19:40.078
right before the election.

00:19:40.078 --> 00:19:41.613
And this is a little bit strange

00:19:41.613 --> 00:19:44.383
because nonprofits
are by law forbidden

00:19:44.383 --> 00:19:46.852 align:start size:88% position:13%
from engaging in
explicit electioneering.

00:19:46.852 --> 00:19:49.521
They can generally exhort
people, be a good citizen,

00:19:49.521 --> 00:19:50.756
get out and vote,

00:19:50.756 --> 00:19:52.291
but they're not allowed
to do any politicking

00:19:52.291 --> 00:19:55.160 align:start size:97% position:3%
that will benefit any
particular candidate or party.

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:57.196
And the IRS could not be
more clear about this.

00:19:57.196 --> 00:19:59.965
So, why would you have
this large river of cash

00:19:59.965 --> 00:20:02.768 align:start position:0%
coming from all these
foundations, coming from Soros,

00:20:02.768 --> 00:20:03.936
coming from Warren Buffett,

00:20:03.936 --> 00:20:05.871
flowing into these nonprofits,

00:20:05.871 --> 00:20:08.307
when these nonprofits are
supposed to, as I say,

00:20:08.307 --> 00:20:10.309
be neutrals in the
election process?

00:20:10.309 --> 00:20:13.412
So, I don't see this
as a quote conspiracy.

00:20:13.412 --> 00:20:16.515 align:start size:97% position:3%
What I see, rather, going
on is there's a coordination

00:20:16.515 --> 00:20:18.417 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
on the left and
among the Democrats

00:20:18.417 --> 00:20:20.252 line:0%
to sort of enable the heist.

00:20:20.252 --> 00:20:21.887 line:0%
So, consider, like,
Mark Zuckerberg.

00:20:21.887 --> 00:20:23.188 line:0%
He puts all this money in,

00:20:23.188 --> 00:20:25.724
and he uses it as
financial leverage

00:20:25.724 --> 00:20:28.060
to get all these
mail in drop boxes.

00:20:28.060 --> 00:20:29.995 align:start size:97% position:3%
Some of these cities weren't
planning on having these,

00:20:29.995 --> 00:20:32.731
this many drop boxes,
but Zuckerberg is,
you want my money,

00:20:32.731 --> 00:20:34.333
you need to put up
all these drop boxes,

00:20:34.333 --> 00:20:35.634
and if you don't do it,

00:20:35.634 --> 00:20:36.935
you're gonna have to
give my money back.

00:20:36.935 --> 00:20:38.870
So you have a private
citizen, unbelievably,

00:20:38.870 --> 00:20:42.441
infiltrating election offices
and using his financial muscle

00:20:42.441 --> 00:20:45.177
to get, to essentially run the
way the election is conducted

00:20:45.177 --> 00:20:46.645
in 2020.

00:20:46.645 --> 00:20:48.580 align:start position:0%
Now, again, I'm not saying
Zuckerberg knew about the mules.

00:20:48.580 --> 00:20:50.315 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm assuming he didn't,
but think of it.

00:20:50.315 --> 00:20:51.550
If he didn't fund
the drop boxes,

00:20:51.550 --> 00:20:54.453 align:start size:84% position:16%
the mules wouldn't
have a place to go to.

00:20:54.453 --> 00:20:57.389 line:0%
- Dinesh, it was
only $400 million

00:20:57.389 --> 00:21:00.025 line:0%
that he personally gave
to fortify the election.

00:21:00.025 --> 00:21:01.927 line:0%
Are you saying $400 million

00:21:01.927 --> 00:21:03.795 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
might have ticked
this thing a little?

00:21:03.795 --> 00:21:05.030
- Dave, you got,

00:21:05.030 --> 00:21:06.865
you're talking to a guy
who spent eight months

00:21:06.865 --> 00:21:10.002 align:start size:88% position:13%
in overnight confinement
for giving $20,000

00:21:10.002 --> 00:21:11.503
to a college friend of mine.

00:21:11.503 --> 00:21:14.406
I was found in violation of
the campaign finance laws.

00:21:14.406 --> 00:21:17.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was basically, you
know, locked up overnight.

00:21:17.676 --> 00:21:20.178 align:start size:81% position:19%
So, when I see the
amount of money

00:21:20.178 --> 00:21:22.648
that these guys are able to
put in, now, quite frankly,

00:21:22.648 --> 00:21:24.683
the, part of the genius
of what Zuckerberg did is

00:21:24.683 --> 00:21:28.053
I can't find a law that
says you can't do that.

00:21:28.053 --> 00:21:30.355
I think, in a way, the
audacity of that move

00:21:30.355 --> 00:21:33.925 align:start position:0%
is that nobody even anticipated
that actual state laws

00:21:33.925 --> 00:21:36.395 align:start size:97% position:3%
that govern elections could
somehow be manipulated

00:21:36.395 --> 00:21:38.497
from the outside,
by a guy coming in,

00:21:38.497 --> 00:21:40.132
essentially, with a
sack full of cash.

00:21:40.132 --> 00:21:42.467
So, see all of that
enabled the heist,

00:21:42.467 --> 00:21:44.102
